00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:29.900
{last frame of OP}

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.470
What terrible table manners.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:36.740
Seventh Episode 「Women」

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:37.010
Eat it in thirty minutes and they get 20,000 yen, huh?

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.920
So that means they'll get 40,000 yen per hour.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.510
Is that kind of income necessary?

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.500
It's a good income for a woman.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.210
Hey, Murasaki-chan, am I a good woman?

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.090
What's the point of confirming that with a seven-year-old?

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.930
You're a good woman, Tamaki.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:51.860
Aren't I?

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.690
You gave me an electric stove.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.090
I did, didn't I?

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.350
I'm not talking about being a good or bad person.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.020
I'm asking if I'm a woman who can be loved.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.830
How should we know?

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.720
What do you think, Yamie?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.810
Do you think I'm interested in any other women besides myself?

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.900
Hey, do you know where to find a good man?

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.030
There is one!

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.790
Shinkurou is a good man.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.460
Shinkurou-kun, eh?

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.750
He's kind!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.340
But that's all he is.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.620
He's strong, too.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.820
I guess he does pass several requirements, now that I think about it.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.890
But being a lolicon is a problem, after all.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.080
Lolicon?

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.300
It means that he loves you.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.340
It's time already.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.010
I have to go to university.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.430
How rare.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:41.440
Don't you always sleep in until noon and then loiter around?

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.770
I have to meet someone today.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.520
Isn't university a place you go to study?

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.620
That's not all there is to it.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.460
You shouldn't be watching TV all the time,

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.480
and instead go out and play with men more, now that you have the chance.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.830
I play with Shinkurou.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:02.490
But I have nothing else to do but watch TV until he comes home.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.610
How about coming to my university with me?

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:08.080
But Shinkurou...

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.790
You should go outside sometimes.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.640
He always gets angry at me, though.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.220
If you're always doing what you're told to by men,

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.550
they'll just use you and throw you aside later.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.830
That's like being a toy, then!

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.540
Right, that's it!

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.930
So you <i>do</i> get it.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:28.150
Anyway, it just means that women should be more assertive.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.560
Okay...

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:34.010
As long as you come home before the boy comes back, you can do whatever you want.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:37.040
If he calls, I'll cover for you.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.460
Really?

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.570
Come on, let's go.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.140
I finally got myself some Bikyaku jeans.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.210
There are Bikyaku jeans for men too?

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.210
Again?

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.230
Of course! Right, Shinkurou?

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:48.800
Yeah.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.300
Oh? I'll get some too.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.000
What are you doing?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.370
It's cool though, you know.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.640
The leggings are weird, though.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.280
No good.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.130
Ah, yeah, it wasn't good.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:58.890
Why?

00:03:58.890 --> 00:03:59.780
This isn't happening.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.810
Right, it's not happening.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.080
They look like they're hard to walk in.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.680
Yeah, that's it.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:04.260
Hello?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.680
What'd you say?

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.540
Never mind that, the snacks you bought were too sweet.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.600
I'm telling you, it doesn't suit my tastes.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.680
Don't you understand?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.770
Ah, I borrowed this cellphone earlier.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.020
She's in Tamaki's room.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.120
She's teaching her the joys of being a woman or something.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.680
I don't know.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.780
Anyway, the soy sauce was bad.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.460
You've got to buy the nice and expensive ones.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.480
I'm not talking about that.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.820
Murasaki is in Tamaki's room, right?

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.370
That's fine, then.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.890
No, enough of that story.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.720
Yes, yes, yes.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.500
Hey, those are my underwear!

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.440
You have a woman wash your underwear?

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.690
No!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.770
What's that?

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.750
That's their style of fashion.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.180
Aren't they cold?

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.490
They've got spirit, so they're probably fine.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.540
At Shinkurou's school, everyone wore the same clothes.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.370
So, is everyone free to choose here?

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.340
That's because it's university.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.880
I see, freedom is good.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.880
It reeks of mold.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.080
It always reeks of mold when you're around.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.430
You're wearing the same kind of clothes as usual.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.930
Does she have spirit with these clothes, too?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.370
No, no, she's being <i>too </i>assertive.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:29.670
What'd you say?

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.210
She's like an adult video star or some cabaret singer.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.350
What's that?

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.360
You're saying that in front of a child?

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.050
Her nails are short, so maybe she's more of an adult video star.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.070
Or are these extensions?

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.180
They broke!

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.320
Did you fight with your boyfriend or something?

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.480
You know, I'll never forgive you.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.160
I don't want to be told that by a thief!

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.660
You've had several men stolen from you.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.660
Shut up!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.660
You always steal my men,

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.750
and then throw them aside in the end!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.050
Those men just weren't enough for me.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.760
That's because you're too half-baked.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:05:59.770
I can't help it.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.410
They're the ones who chose me in the first place.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.470
They're just being deceived!

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:06.130
This person is really loud, Tamaki.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:06.950
Isn't she?

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.070
Be quiet, child.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.510
I think those clothes are strange.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.740
What'd you say?

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.890
They're too flashy, and it's like a balloon!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:14.540
Ball-

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.220
I can see your panties too, it's just very unladylike.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.430
What a cheeky kid!

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.730
It's your new boyfriend's tastes, right?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.630
Shut up!

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.800
Introduce him to me.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.460
I would never!

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.530
I can imagine who it is, though.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:28.930
What are you saying?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.150
The one that's a year below you in the tennis club.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.770
Shinozaki-kun, was it?

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:35.330
You...

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.100
Let me give you some advice.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.790
He likes long kisses.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.030
Tamaki...

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.840
He likes it slow and to take his time.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.460
You have to stretch a bit to reach because he's tall,

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.450
but that's what's nice about it.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.850
He wrapped his arms around my waist and embraced...

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.480
Are you okay, Tamaki?

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.410
Being beautiful is a sin.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.970
Is university a place where you compete for men?

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.780
That happens everywhere.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.490
Is that how it is?

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.860
There aren't any seats.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:17.010
Geez, they should go off campus and do it.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:19.930
Is university a place to find a companion?

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:23.170
It's not something that extreme, but it's a place where you can do that.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.260
Everyone looks like they're having fun.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:30.310
You don't know what they're thinking deep inside, though.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.890
They might be looking for new prey.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.220
What's prey?

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:38.350
It means that men find other women, and women find other men.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.350
Women too?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.720
Naturally.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:45.150
And charming women like me draw men in from everywhere.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.040
How many?

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.700
I guess the number of digits you have.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:48.590
Ten?

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:50.390
Digits aren't only on your hand.

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:51.200
That many?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:51.780
Yep.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.450
That's how you pursue your ideal man.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:08:00.060
Is that the freedom my mother spoke of?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.130
What was that?

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.770
Nothing.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:06.960
She's giving him a present.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.740
Those kinds of couples break up right away.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:10.470
Why?

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.960
One of them's forcing himself to keep up with the other.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.770
There aren't any humans who are the same, after all.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:17.750
What about the couples over there?

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.480
That man is a pimp.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.660
That woman is like, "Hang in there a bit longer."

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:25.440
He'll soon get used and thrown aside, though.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:29.030
You're amazing, Tamaki! You're like a fortune teller.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.660
I'm more trustworthy than a fortune teller, though.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.280
I'm the love doctor, after all.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.260
Tamaki.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:37.490
You're late, Satoshi.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.000
I almost thought of going to class, too.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:40.420
Sorry.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:44.350
I have to look after her today, though.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:45.550
So could we meet again next time?

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.220
I had something to tell you today, though.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:51.590
You can't tell me next week?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.160
Well, what I have to tell you is really quick.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.150
That's why I'm saying...

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.270
You...

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:58.600
You brought her on purpose, didn't you?

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.420
What are you saying?

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.230
Because on the phone-

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.530
That's not it!

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.530
You're always like this.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:04.850
She's from the room next door-

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:05.720
Let's...

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.050
Let's talk next week.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:07.920
Let's end this toda-

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.760
Not today, Satoshi!

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:10.570
I can't go on-

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:11.450
Stop!

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.490
I can't keep up with you.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.280
You're always selfish.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.040
How? There are times when I try to keep up with you too!

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.900
And when was that?

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.020
Hey, are you serious?

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.030
Well...

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.830
I seem strong because you're weak!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:29.100
That's like saying I can't be strong!

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.690
No! I'm trying, too!

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.910
But then you say it doesn't matter and start yelling!

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:34.940
You do that too!

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.900
I'm always being held back.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.310
That can't be helped! You...

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.510
There are things I can do, too!

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.210
But, with you...

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:45.380
There are times when I want you to protect me too!

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.050
That's impossible.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:50.140
Whenever I try to do something, you get upset and hit me.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.860
That's because you're not decisive!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.880
That's why I said on the phone that I'd tell you clearly.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.390
Not that!

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:58.130
You even brought this kid.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.400
Let's talk about this next time!

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.050
Let's have a proper talk!

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:05.060
I won't be seeing you anymore.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:06.070
Satoshi...

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:07.040
I'll be clear.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.460
Let's break up.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:12.090
No way, this is it for us?

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.670
It's what I want.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.490
All right, let's have a long talk now.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.250
I'm telling you, there's nothing else to talk about.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.570
Even if you don't have anything to say, I do!

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:24.100
You have to look after her, don't you, Tamaki?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.140
It's all right!

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.810
It's not!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:30.040
Plus, I don't want to hear anymore.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:32.240
Anyway, I'm going now.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.310
Hold it!

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.530
Being violent again?

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.340
I said, let's talk!

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.270
Stop!

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:38.660
Don't go!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.670
I want to be freed from you.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:43.960
I can't stand it anymore.

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.760
Give me a break already!

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.450
Satoshi...

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.990
Please let me go!

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:56.970
Sorry...

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:00.930
Tamaki?

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.820
Tamaki?

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.710
Aren't you going to drink your juice?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:12.340
The ice is melting.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.580
I'm watering it down.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:14.890
I see.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:17.370
Murasaki-chan.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:19.610
Is the juice good?

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.980
Yeah, it's good.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:22.510
That's great.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.620
You can drink a lot, okay?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.700
Tamaki.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.250
Veggie juice is good too.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.640
Are you okay?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:31.780
Perfectly fine.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:32.800
Cheer up.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.210
I am cheerful.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.090
I was dumped,

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:42.510
but I actually wanted to find a man first and then break up with him.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.330
I see, you're great.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.440
You don't hold back with men or try to dress how they want.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.940
It's okay to hold back or to have a paired look.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.530
You more or less have to respect and accept them.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:59.350
You're a good woman, though.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:01.990
No, you're a kind <i>and</i> good person!

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.670
Namely, you're good on the inside!

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:06.370
That kind of woman is a woman that can be loved.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:08.720
Murasaki-chan.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:11.750
You're a far better woman than I am.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.760
I wish I could treat you to beer at times like this.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.800
But I can't do that as I am now.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.180
I'm a good woman too!

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:24.010
Maybe it's because I'm too charming.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:27.220
That's right! You're a woman overflowing with charm!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.390
Right?

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.270
Even a woman like me would fall in love with you!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:30.920
Right?

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:31.350
Yeah!

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.690
There are countless men.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:35.610
I've got to find the man for me.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.440
Yeah, I'll look for one too.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.590
Let's see, is there anyone?

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:42.620
Is there anyone?

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.620
There is! Here, and over there too!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.210
Is there anyone? Is there anyone?

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:55.920
Good man, found!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.820
Tamaki, over there-

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.280
Tamaki?

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.770
Murasaki-chan.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:04.000
Yes.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:10.430
You know, men fool women who seem loose and weak off the bat.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.770
Fool them?

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:17.870
I changed my hairstyle and clothing style, too.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:20.280
I even thought to myself, should I be thinner or not?

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.280
You're really cool, though, Tamaki!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.400
It doesn't matter.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:28.950
Even for strong women, if they can't rely on a man, it's hopeless.

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:32.700
There's no point in relying on them if you can do it yourself.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:38.090
Even if you're useless, it's hopeless if you don't have an attitude like, "I'm doing my best for you!"

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.130
"Doing my best?"

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:44.560
Even though a man doesn't need it and even though it won't look good on him,

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:47.460
they prefer the girls who make them a hand-knit muffler.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.970
Those kind of women are the best in the end.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.730
Those kind of women?

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:56.400
The ones who are a bit loose, a bit excessive, and kind of hang on to you.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.440
And their singing is kind of terrible.

00:13:58.840 --> 00:13:59.850
That's right.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:01.360
That's dangerous.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.410
That's right.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:08.450
Those kinds of women always act familiar and are good at showing off how useful they are.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:12.080
Women who act familiar and seem useful...

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.510
Do you have a cold?

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.690
No, it just kind of came on.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.530
I see.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.970
Anyway,

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.010
there's something I want to give you.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.010
Here.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:30.220
Um... what's this?

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.480
A wool hand warmer!

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:37.520
I went to the post office the other day,

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.820
and thought of it when I saw the work place.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.530
I thought to myself, "This is it!"

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:44.600
This?

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:49.740
Yes, but I added my own original touch and made it out of wool.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.990
Wool, huh?

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.130
After I went to your room the other day, I thought to myself,

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.450
"Aren't the nights cold?"

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:01.660
You don't need it?

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:04.380
No! Of course not!

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.340
Now I won't be cold anymore!

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:09.120
But if you don't like it...

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.620
Not at all!

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:12.360
They look really warm, too.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.280
I see!

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.320
Thank goodness.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.570
You can use them at school, too.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:18.570
At school?!

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:19.670
You don't want to?

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:23.850
No, I just thought I'd treasure them and use them at home.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:27.860
It's okay, if they get worn out, I'll make you new ones.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.620
Oh no, Shinkurou!

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.080
He's being deceived by a woman who acts familiar and useful!

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:38.920
Hey!

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:42.460
Sorry!

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:46.760
I'm in a hurry, so please excuse me.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.210
Hold on.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.360
Sorry, I'm in a hurry.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:51.800
Go ahead.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.060
Excuse me, the bill please.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.270
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.640
It can't be, she...

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.170
You can't do that, she's only seven years old.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:02.290
Seven years old?

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.130
Here's your bill, miss.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.030
Yes, yes.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.780
Hurry up, Tamaki!

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:09.270
Wait a bit, Murasaki-chan!

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:10.490
Murasaki?

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:12.800
Are you a lolicon, mister?

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.520
Your bill comes to 1280 yen.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.890
1200 and how much?

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.290
1280 yen.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.540
Okay.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.150
1280 yen received.

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.260
Thank you very much.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:29.770
Sorry for the wait.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:30.530
You're so slow!

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:32.220
Hey, hold it!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.680
Excuse me, the bill please.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.390
Yes, we'll take your sales slip.

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:38.230
You confirmed it on the phone, though!

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:40.980
That was several hours ago.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.370
That's true, but...

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:46.650
Couldn't you at least think of why I had called?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:50.400
I am not her guardian, so I have no responsibility.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.610
Tamaki-san took her out, right?

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.650
Probably.

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:55.740
Where?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:56.640
I don't know.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:59.390
What places would Tamaki-san likely go to?

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.090
Who knows?

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:02.880
Then where does she always go?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.230
Dr. Arai's Buddhist temple, maybe?

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.690
Buddhist temple?

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:08.730
Tamaki-san went there?

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:10.130
I often go there.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.130
You're doing this on purpose, aren't you?

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.330
I'm just answering your questions.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:15.720
Shinkurou!

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:17.560
Murasaki!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:18.560
I need to talk to you.

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:21.010
I'm the one that needs to talk to you!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:21.780
Where'd you go?

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.390
Forget that, I have something more important to discuss.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:27.690
Shinkurou, break up with Yuuno right this instant.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.070
Wh-What'd you say?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.730
Yuuno is a deceiving woman!

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:34.490
Her image of being a loose and useful woman is a farce!

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.220
What are you saying?

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.960
I'm a better woman than anyone!

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:40.410
That's why you became a lolicon, right?

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.070
Who's a lolicon?!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.500
Tamaki-san put some more strange ideas into your mind again, didn't she?

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.210
I'm saying you'll be unhappy if you choose a cheap woman who acts familiar!

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.890
Familiar?

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:51.220
You mean yourself?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:54.660
How insolent! I'm not a cheap woman!

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:58.100
Just how should I say it so that you understand? This is getting on my nerves!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.130
Today you'll be happy.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:04.730
Tomorrow you'll be happy, too.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.100
I'm sure my luck will be good tomorrow.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.190
It has to be good.

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:19.730
She seems to be living in an old apartment named Samidare,

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:22.790
and there's one woman on guard at a love hotel across from it.

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:24.480
Benika's subordinate?

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:27.420
It is most likely Inuzuka Yayoi.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.510
She must be inconvenienced living at an old apartment.

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:35.000
I'm not sure of Benika's motives,

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.620
but I'm concerned about Souju-sama's relation with her.

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:38.590
Souju?

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.930
Benika handled the security for the Inner Sanctuary.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:50.160
It was a mistake to leave her alone with Souju so that she would have someone to talk to and be distracted by.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:54.450
She put into her mind everything there was about the world outside.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:57.710
Does it hurt?

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:02.820
Compared to pains of the heart, this is nothing.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.500
I come to see you, just like I am now, don't I?

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:08.330
I can't even meet the one I love.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:12.930
I was pulled away from my most beloved daughter who was conceived with that person.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:16.800
Do I have to continue to accept this fate and live on?

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.160
Murasaki is Kazuko's child.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:23.130
Don't ever say that she is your daughter again.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:27.230
If I could live with her, I wouldn't mind making the Kuhouins my enemy.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.860
Don't be foolish.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:33.940
Do you want to see my suffering that much?

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:38.690
You are the only woman I have ever loved.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:42.330
Please endure with that.

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.460
If I had lived a normal life,

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.730
I could have lived with the one I loved, had a child,

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:52.750
loved it, raised it, and shown it the happiness of a family.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.450
And I can't even do that.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:58.140
In its place, the Kuhouins have no inconveniences.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:01.740
By having no inconveniences, there is no freedom in its stead.

00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:06.350
Do you not see Murasaki as your own daughter?

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:11.360
I was born with the blood of a Kuhouin.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.150
By placing my daughter in the Inner Sanctuary,

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:17.310
it is my answer to how I feel for my daughter.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.350
I see.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:23.990
So she is nothing but the family's priestess.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.360
No!

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:34.530
Souju-sama! Souju-sama!

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:37.720
Quickly, take Murasaki outside!

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:37.720
Souju-sama! Souju-sama!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.570
No, let me go!

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.360
Souju-sama!

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:42.380
Souju-sama!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.430
Holding onto a Hina doll and dying...

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.770
She's a detestable woman right until the end.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.770
Note: A Hina doll is used to pray for one's daughter's fortune.

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:50.940
Stop it!

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:54.520
Just how miserable do you want to make me?!

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.030
How cruel can you be?!

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:59.710
Just what am I to you?!

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:06.120
Hurry up and carry Souju out!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.040
It couldn't be helped.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.430
It couldn't be helped, you say?

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:20.070
I can only see the Inner Sanctuary as an illusion.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.990
Illusions will eventually be brought back to reality and be crushed.

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:28.060
So that's why I wanted to slowly show her a bit of reality.

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:29.730
And that led Souju astray.

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:31.980
I couldn't stand seeing her like that anymore.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.940
As of today, you will leave this house.

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:36.390
I was going to, even if you didn't tell me to.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:37.980
It's making me go crazy too.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.690
I will not permit any further utterances that defile the Kuhouins!

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:43.050
I'm disappointed in you.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.680
I thought you would've done something more.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.850
Leave.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:10.930
Murasaki had found out that Souju was her real mother.

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:16.980
However, she couldn't possibly have entrusted her feelings to Murasaki.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:22.920
No matter what Benika may do, the fate of a Kuhouin woman will not change.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.530
What shall we do?

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:29.210
Bring back Murasaki without creating a disturbance, if possible.

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:30.530
Yes.

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:34.160
This will put an end to my mistakes.

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:38.120
An end... to it all.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:06.860
sonna ni asette sa nani mo kamo shiritai to omowanaide

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:06.860
そんなに焦ってさ何もかも知りたいと思わないで

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:06.860
Rushing so much, don't think that you want to know everything.

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:02.610
{last frame of Kimono}

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:12.990
kimi dake no RIZUMU de tokiakashite ikeba ii

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:12.990
君だけのリズムで解き明かしていけばいい

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:12.990
Just figure it out in your own rhythm.

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:16.580
demo ne chotto dake isoide sagashita houga ii kamo ne

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:16.580
でもねちょっとだけ急いで探した方がいいかもね

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:16.580
But it's probably better to rush and search just a little.

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:19.580
sunadokei to isshou ni SARASARA ochite yuku genjitsu to

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:19.580
砂時計と一緒にサラサラ落ちてゆく現実と

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:19.580
Along with the reality that gently falls with the hourglass.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.080
futte kuru mirai kasanaru shunkan ichido daketo

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.080
降ってくる未来重なる瞬間一度だけと

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.080
The moment the raining future overlaps occurs only once.

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:26.000
sou kizuita

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:26.000
そう気付いた

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:26.000
I realized that.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:33.140
hatenaku toumei na jiyuu ni iro o tsukete ikou It's my way

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:33.140
果てなく透明な自由に色をつけていこう It's my way

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:33.140
Let's color the endlessly transparent freedom: it's my way.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:39.270
kousa suru IMEEJI kanji nagara sa

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:39.270
交差するイメージ感じながらさ

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:39.270
As we feel the crossing image.

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:46.400
kimi no yuku michi no kiseki ni sotto yorisoinagara we can take

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:46.400
君の行く道の軌跡にそっと寄り添いながら we can take

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:46.400
As we quietly snuggle up to the miracle on your path: we can take

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:52.200
betsubetsu no RAIN tadotte iku yo

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:52.200
別々のラインたどっていくよ

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:52.200
Tracing separate lines.

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:57.200
Crossing days.

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:56.450
I forget something that I want

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:59.910
try to get something important

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:03.210
I forgot something that I want

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:06.460
try to get something important

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:20.020
Next on kurenai:

00:24:20.590 --> 00:24:24.820
Taking Care of Oneself and Cowardice.
